WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:03.070
The Foundation was in chaos.

00:00:03.070 --> 00:00:07.650
One minute, Dr. Bright was looking into some
harmless products on Amazon to help the Foundation's

00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:10.730
anomalies have a nicer experience in their
cells.

00:00:10.730 --> 00:00:14.900
The next, he was physically fighting for his
life against the company's CEO.

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:20.050
Of course, Dr. Bright’s wacky antics had
revealed the location of the SCP Foundation’s

00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:26.149
most valuable containment site to Jeff Bezos
and his legions of minions.

00:00:26.149 --> 00:00:31.079
Does Dr. Jack Bright have it in him to fix
his mistake, defeat the mighty Jeff Bezos,

00:00:31.079 --> 00:00:33.640
and save the SCP Foundation from corporate
servitude?

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:38.800
Are the forces of the SCP Foundation equal
in strength to the Amazon horde?

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:48.870
And how, at the eleventh hour, will anomalies
like SCP-096, SCP-682, SCP-173, and SCP-049

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:50.379
help save the day?

00:00:50.379 --> 00:00:51.379
Buckle up.

00:00:51.379 --> 00:00:54.899
The only way to find out is to keep watching.

00:00:54.899 --> 00:00:59.949
The two titans, Dr. Bright and the freakishly
buff Jeff Bezos, were locked into an intense

00:00:59.949 --> 00:01:00.949
struggle.

00:01:00.949 --> 00:01:04.950
The hapless immortal tried his best to punch
and kick the augmented CEO, but all it did

00:01:04.950 --> 00:01:06.720
was make Bezos laugh.

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:09.300
“Pathetic, Jack,” Bezos roared.

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:12.780
“Let me show you how a real man does it.”

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:17.950
With one punch, Bezos sent Dr. Bright skidding
across the dirt, seeing stars.

00:01:17.950 --> 00:01:22.940
Bezos punched him so hard, Dr. Bright felt
like he’d been hit by a runaway truck.

00:01:22.940 --> 00:01:26.330
Where had he even gotten all this anomalous
technology?

00:01:26.330 --> 00:01:28.390
Something more was going on here...

00:01:28.390 --> 00:01:33.150
But before Dr. Bright could collect his thoughts,
Bezos was already upon him.

00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:37.560
The ruthless business mogul clasped his hands
together and brought them down onto the back

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:42.340
of Jack’s head in a brutal pile drive, burying
his head in the dirt.

00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:47.200
The guards of Site-19 looked on in terror
at the thousands of Amazon troops surrounding

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:50.400
them - And they were betting all this on a
fist fight?

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:55.270
And what’s more, it didn’t look like Dr.
Bright was winning that fist fight.

00:01:55.270 --> 00:01:58.190
Unless the good doctor used his special move.

00:01:58.190 --> 00:02:02.620
Bezos, still cackling like a Saturday morning
cartoon villain, grabbed Dr. Bright by his

00:02:02.620 --> 00:02:04.960
hair and dragged him out of the dirt.

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:08.380
He lifted the Doctor, bloody and bashed, with
one hand.

00:02:08.380 --> 00:02:13.360
At that moment, Dr. Bright knew that he had
to go with the nuclear option here - he needed

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:19.870
to use SCP-963 to take over the body of Jeff
Bezos and end this demented war.

00:02:19.870 --> 00:02:21.430
“Had enough, Jack?”

00:02:21.430 --> 00:02:22.470
Bezos said.

00:02:22.470 --> 00:02:27.240
“Or do you want me to humiliate you even
more in front of your sad little employees?

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:32.390
Or, should I say, my sad little employees!”

00:02:32.390 --> 00:02:36.620
Without another word, Dr. Bright grabbed the
amulet hanging around his neck and balled

00:02:36.620 --> 00:02:38.250
it into his fist.

00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:42.170
Moving as quickly as he could, he lunged at
Bezos with the medallion, knowing that one

00:02:42.170 --> 00:02:45.070
touch should be enough to finish this whole
thing.

00:02:45.070 --> 00:02:49.900
But then, the unexpected happened: Bezos caught
Dr. Bright’s hand.

00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:53.350
The flesh of the CEO’s fist turned obsidian
black.

00:02:53.350 --> 00:02:55.150
He gave a cruel smirk.

00:02:55.150 --> 00:02:57.310
He was still himself.

00:02:57.310 --> 00:02:58.620
Impossible…

00:02:58.620 --> 00:03:02.930
All the SCP Foundation staff in attendance
were shocked and horrified, but none more

00:03:02.930 --> 00:03:05.210
than Dr. Bright himself.

00:03:05.210 --> 00:03:10.210
This was the first time that SCP-963 simply
hadn’t worked!

00:03:10.210 --> 00:03:15.180
“I don’t understand,” Jack said, voice
trembling as Bezos squeezed his hand with

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:16.180
an iron grip.

00:03:16.180 --> 00:03:17.420
“I should have taken you over.

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:18.520
How is this possible?”

00:03:18.520 --> 00:03:23.069
Bezos chuckled before unleashing a brutal
headbutt on Dr. Bright, throwing him back

00:03:23.069 --> 00:03:24.360
through the air.

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:28.420
Bright was lucky he managed to keep a grip
on the medallion - this body hadn’t worn

00:03:28.420 --> 00:03:33.610
it for thirty days; if he dropped it, he would
have just been another useless necklace.

00:03:33.610 --> 00:03:34.990
“Nanomachines, son!”

00:03:34.990 --> 00:03:38.090
Bezos barked, cracking his neck back into
place.

00:03:38.090 --> 00:03:40.540
“I had them designed with you in mind.

00:03:40.540 --> 00:03:44.470
Any time and anywhere your necklace touches
me, they reshuffle my genetics to turn that

00:03:44.470 --> 00:03:46.690
flesh into inanimate psuedometal.

00:03:46.690 --> 00:03:50.440
Do you think I’d lead an assault on the
SCP Foundation without planning for every

00:03:50.440 --> 00:03:51.550
possible eventuality?

00:03:51.550 --> 00:03:53.780
I’ve been playing the long game!”

00:03:53.780 --> 00:03:57.880
It was at this point that the Foundation guards
assembled outside the building opened fire

00:03:57.880 --> 00:04:00.819
on Bezos, but it was no use.

00:04:00.819 --> 00:04:04.680
The bullets just ricocheted off of his anomalously
enhanced physique.

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:09.190
He just gave a bellowing laugh and ordered
the full strength of his forces to move in.

00:04:09.190 --> 00:04:12.890
As far as he was concerned, the fight was
already won.

00:04:12.890 --> 00:04:19.180
If their forces could plant the grinning Amazon
flag in the heart of Site-19, the SCP Foundation

00:04:19.180 --> 00:04:20.559
would be his.

00:04:20.559 --> 00:04:23.680
It was time for the true final battle to begin.

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:28.520
Amazon’s troops loaded their weapons and
charged, firing volley after volley of bullets

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:31.939
onto the Foundation guards entrenched in their
positions.

00:04:31.939 --> 00:04:36.520
Of course, the Foundation personnel was better
trained, but the Amazon army outnumbered them

00:04:36.520 --> 00:04:37.729
ten to one.

00:04:37.729 --> 00:04:42.879
It was only a matter of time until the barricades
gave way, and the forces spilled into the

00:04:42.879 --> 00:04:44.759
containment facility.

00:04:44.759 --> 00:04:46.979
And then they did.

00:04:46.979 --> 00:04:51.110
Inside the building, Dr. Clef was reading
his new copy of Shotguns: A Comprehensive

00:04:51.110 --> 00:04:53.199
Guide, when the army breached the perimeter.

00:04:53.199 --> 00:04:57.860
It was at this point that he put down the
book and picked up his favorite shotgun, a

00:04:57.860 --> 00:05:03.490
Remington Model 11-87 - fun fact: Also the
preferred weapon of Anton Chigurh from No

00:05:03.490 --> 00:05:06.650
Country For Old Men - and entered the fray.

00:05:06.650 --> 00:05:11.419
They’d need every SCP Foundation hand on
deck to repel the incoming attack.

00:05:11.419 --> 00:05:17.139
The one thing that not even Dr. Clef predicted
was for the anomalies to get involved, too.

00:05:17.139 --> 00:05:21.830
You see, in ordering his troops to attack
Site-19, the fleet of Amazon attack helicopters

00:05:21.830 --> 00:05:27.439
above began launching AGM-114 Hellfire missiles
at the building to knock out guard towers

00:05:27.439 --> 00:05:29.879
and strategic communications arrays.

00:05:29.879 --> 00:05:34.860
This, however, had the unintended effect of
causing power fluctuations within the building,

00:05:34.860 --> 00:05:39.300
and with so many of the reserve generators
devoted to maintaining external security against

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:43.460
the Amazon army, internal security failed
entirely.

00:05:43.460 --> 00:05:47.550
In other words, a whole lot of cell doors
were popping open.

00:05:47.550 --> 00:05:52.509
A group of Amazon footsoldiers was making
their way down hallway 6C when they saw something

00:05:52.509 --> 00:05:58.789
strange on the ground: A tide of green, bubbling
chemicals that produced a horrific smell.

00:05:58.789 --> 00:06:04.379
Little did they know, this was powerful hydrochloric
acid, but in this instance, it wasn’t the

00:06:04.379 --> 00:06:06.330
acid that they should be worried about.

00:06:06.330 --> 00:06:09.680
They heard a raspy voice behind them say...

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:10.990
“Disssgussssting...”

00:06:10.990 --> 00:06:17.670
That’s when they turned to see SCP-682,
the giant, rage-fueled immortal reptile, standing

00:06:17.670 --> 00:06:18.839
right behind them.

00:06:18.839 --> 00:06:25.189
It had just finished its exotic beef jerky
collection, and now, it was eager for seconds.

00:06:25.189 --> 00:06:29.669
The Amazon soldiers panicked and began to
open fire on the beast, but all that succeeded

00:06:29.669 --> 00:06:32.029
in doing was annoying it.

00:06:32.029 --> 00:06:37.630
SCP-682 leaped onto them and began devouring
the group of hapless mercenaries alive.

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:41.860
Elsewhere in the facility, another group of
Amazon mercenaries was chasing some defenseless

00:06:41.860 --> 00:06:46.039
SCP Foundation researchers through the secure
humanoid containment wing.

00:06:46.039 --> 00:06:49.939
The researchers tried to run, but soon, they
were backed into a corner.

00:06:49.939 --> 00:06:53.090
The mercenaries laughed and leveled their
assault rifles.

00:06:53.090 --> 00:06:54.729
This would be an easy kill.

00:06:54.729 --> 00:07:00.240
However, the second they tried to fire, they
realized something extremely strange had occurred:

00:07:00.240 --> 00:07:04.240
All of their guns had turned into delightful
bouquets.

00:07:04.240 --> 00:07:10.159
Standing between them and the researchers
they intended to kill was SCP-343, also known

00:07:10.159 --> 00:07:12.130
to some as God.

00:07:12.130 --> 00:07:16.999
“Now, now, boys,” SCP-343 said with a
slight smile.

00:07:16.999 --> 00:07:19.990
“Can’t we all just get along?

00:07:19.990 --> 00:07:21.979
Make love, not war.”

00:07:21.979 --> 00:07:26.349
Frightened by the seemingly impossible act
they just witnessed, the now unarmed mercenaries

00:07:26.349 --> 00:07:30.710
ran into a nearby room with a sturdy-looking
door and locked themselves in.

00:07:30.710 --> 00:07:33.050
Hopefully, nobody would get them here.

00:07:33.050 --> 00:07:37.559
That thought was interrupted by a grandiose
voice with an archaic French accent speaking

00:07:37.559 --> 00:07:38.710
out behind them.

00:07:38.710 --> 00:07:41.180
“Why hello there, good sirs!

00:07:41.180 --> 00:07:44.099
So kind of you to step into my practice today.”

00:07:44.099 --> 00:07:49.060
They turned and saw a strange, robed man wearing
a runner pigeon mask.

00:07:49.060 --> 00:07:53.979
The figure removed the mask, only to reveal
what seemed like another strange beaked mask

00:07:53.979 --> 00:07:54.979
underneath.

00:07:54.979 --> 00:08:01.009
It was SCP-049, his desk covered in pleasingly-polished
Amazon medical tools.

00:08:01.009 --> 00:08:05.000
“My, my, you gents seem a little under the
weather.

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:08.979
This is a cause for concern,” the Plague
Doctor said as he began to walk toward the

00:08:08.979 --> 00:08:09.979
frightened mercenaries.

00:08:09.979 --> 00:08:12.349
“The Pestilence runs rife these days.

00:08:12.349 --> 00:08:13.779
Not to worry, though.

00:08:13.779 --> 00:08:14.860
I’m an expert.

00:08:14.860 --> 00:08:19.620
And I’ve been itching to try out my lovely
new tools...”

00:08:19.620 --> 00:08:24.229
Horrified screaming was heard from the room
shortly after, then silence.

00:08:24.229 --> 00:08:26.179
But Amazon troops kept pouring in.

00:08:26.179 --> 00:08:30.889
It was an all-out assault beyond any that
Site-19 had ever experienced.

00:08:30.889 --> 00:08:34.399
Some Amazon strike teams were making their
way through the break rooms, hunting for more

00:08:34.399 --> 00:08:37.509
Foundation employees to capture or execute.

00:08:37.509 --> 00:08:42.440
One of them remarked that these SCP Foundation
employees must be real headcases - Why else

00:08:42.440 --> 00:08:46.070
would they keep such a hideous concrete sculpture
in their break room?

00:08:46.070 --> 00:08:47.170
Utterly bizarre.

00:08:47.170 --> 00:08:51.399
The second they found there was no one inside
and turned to leave the room, they all lay

00:08:51.399 --> 00:08:54.139
dead on the ground with snapped necks.

00:08:54.139 --> 00:08:58.490
That would make it seventeen Amazon mercenaries
they’d killed today - The Sculpture was

00:08:58.490 --> 00:09:01.010
having a truly wonderful time.

00:09:01.010 --> 00:09:05.000
Meanwhile, over in his office, Dr. Clef was
fighting for his life.

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:09.220
A group of junior researchers were taking
refuge in there with him and handing him shotgun

00:09:09.220 --> 00:09:13.830
shells from his many, many boxes of them when
he needed to reload.

00:09:13.830 --> 00:09:18.000
Soldier after soldier was running into the
room, and Clef was using his trusty Remington

00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:23.040
pump-action to blow them away with incredible
precision every time one of them ran in.

00:09:23.040 --> 00:09:26.740
An awestruck researcher asked, “How good
are you with that thing?”

00:09:26.740 --> 00:09:30.149
Clef laughed and said, “Kid, I could unbutton
your lab coat with it.”

00:09:30.149 --> 00:09:33.520
But then tragedy struck: Dr. Clef ran out
of shells.

00:09:33.520 --> 00:09:39.170
He sighed and told the assembled researchers
to run out of the back exit and save themselves.

00:09:39.170 --> 00:09:42.339
He’d hold back the tide of Amazon mercenaries
alone.

00:09:42.339 --> 00:09:47.120
He kissed his shotgun and said, “Forgive
me for this, Remy,” then grabbed it by the

00:09:47.120 --> 00:09:48.120
barrel.

00:09:48.120 --> 00:09:51.009
If he couldn’t shoot with it, he’d at
least use it as a club.

00:09:51.009 --> 00:09:56.029
He ran out into the fray, bashing down mercenaries
left and right with his shotgun club until

00:09:56.029 --> 00:09:57.960
he was finally outnumbered.

00:09:57.960 --> 00:10:01.600
A group of heavily-armed soldiers surrounded
him, holding him at gunpoint.

00:10:01.600 --> 00:10:03.360
One of them gave the order to fire.

00:10:03.360 --> 00:10:05.050
“Wait!” Dr. Clef said.

00:10:05.050 --> 00:10:06.879
“I can be valuable to you.

00:10:06.879 --> 00:10:08.190
You don’t know who I am, do you?

00:10:08.190 --> 00:10:10.399
Give me a second; let me show you my ID.”

00:10:10.399 --> 00:10:14.529
Dr. Clef pulled an ID wallet from his lab
coat and showed it to the soldiers.

00:10:14.529 --> 00:10:16.491
They looked at it, confused and a little disturbed.

00:10:16.491 --> 00:10:18.590
The leader of the group said.

00:10:18.590 --> 00:10:20.019
“That’s not an ID card, you schmuck.

00:10:20.019 --> 00:10:21.769
What the hell is that ugly thing anyway?”

00:10:21.769 --> 00:10:24.449
By this point, Dr. Clef had already closed
his eyes.

00:10:24.449 --> 00:10:29.129
A distant screaming got closer and closer,
until the wall of his office exploded.

00:10:29.129 --> 00:10:34.709
SCP-096 entered the room, shrieking with rage,
and began tearing the hapless soldiers to

00:10:34.709 --> 00:10:35.709
shreds.

00:10:35.709 --> 00:10:39.779
Clef rolled away, keeping his eyes closed
and waiting for the carnage to be over.

00:10:39.779 --> 00:10:43.589
But in a grander sense, the carnage had only
just begun.

00:10:43.589 --> 00:10:48.529
Oh, and for those who were curious, yes, SCP-811
did get her blobfish plushy.

00:10:48.529 --> 00:10:50.069
She loved it.

00:10:50.069 --> 00:10:53.769
Outside the facility, Jeff Bezos looked upon
the destruction he wrought and laughed.

00:10:53.769 --> 00:10:57.890
It was just as wonderful as he’d imagined
it in all his years of intense planning for

00:10:57.890 --> 00:10:59.010
this very moment.

00:10:59.010 --> 00:11:02.350
It’d all unfolded exactly to his design.

00:11:02.350 --> 00:11:08.139
The SCP Foundation would fall, and his master
plan would finally be complete.

00:11:08.139 --> 00:11:13.440
Dr. Jack Bright, demoralized but not defeated,
rose shakily to his feet.

00:11:13.440 --> 00:11:15.720
This whole disaster had been his fault.

00:11:15.720 --> 00:11:17.290
Had had to redeem this.

00:11:17.290 --> 00:11:22.759
He had to defeat Jeff Bezos, or the Foundation
would fall into his iron clutches.

00:11:22.759 --> 00:11:27.310
Even if it finally, truly, killed him, Dr.
Bright would not give up.

00:11:27.310 --> 00:11:31.410
“Impressive tech,” Dr. Bright said, cracking
his knuckles and getting Jeff’s attention

00:11:31.410 --> 00:11:32.410
again.

00:11:32.410 --> 00:11:33.940
“Which sweat shop built it for you?”

00:11:33.940 --> 00:11:38.209
Jeff just laughed and turned to Bright again,
more than ready for round two.

00:11:38.209 --> 00:11:42.670
“A little place called Prometheus Labs,
Jack,” Jeff said.

00:11:42.670 --> 00:11:43.670
“Remember them?

00:11:43.670 --> 00:11:46.870
I was on the board of directors before the
incident.

00:11:46.870 --> 00:11:51.560
Just like you and your Foundation dogs, they
left behind plenty of goodies for me.”

00:11:51.560 --> 00:11:54.819
Dr. Bright charged at Bezos, screaming in
animal fury.

00:11:54.819 --> 00:11:58.370
He punched the smug anomalous businessman
square in the jaw.

00:11:58.370 --> 00:12:00.170
Bezos barely even flinched.

00:12:00.170 --> 00:12:04.560
He gave Jack an utterly brutal open-handed
slap, knocking him towards the entrance to

00:12:04.560 --> 00:12:08.829
Site-19, where more Amazon soldiers were still
pouring in.

00:12:08.829 --> 00:12:12.389
Still, Jack began to stand again.

00:12:12.389 --> 00:12:18.089
“What the hell does a corporate stiff like
you want with the SCP Foundation?” he said.

00:12:18.089 --> 00:12:21.100
“We want to help the world, not rule it.”

00:12:21.100 --> 00:12:24.110
Bezos sneered and began stomping toward the
immortal doctor.

00:12:24.110 --> 00:12:26.410
“I don’t just want to rule the world,
Jack.

00:12:26.410 --> 00:12:30.790
I want to hold it in my hand like an apple
and take a big, juicy bite.

00:12:30.790 --> 00:12:37.110
All that exists will belong to me,” he said,
throwing a punch that Dr. Bright was thankfully

00:12:37.110 --> 00:12:38.590
able to dodge.

00:12:38.590 --> 00:12:43.830
“That’s always been the plan, and the
SCP Foundation is the final piece I need.”

00:12:43.830 --> 00:12:49.089
Dr. Bright, summoning all the adrenaline in
his body, unleashed a flurry of sharp punches

00:12:49.089 --> 00:12:50.579
to Jeff’s abdomen.

00:12:50.579 --> 00:12:53.560
He simply tanked every strike and laughed.

00:12:53.560 --> 00:12:56.790
“I’ve been funding the Chaos Insurgency
for years, Jack.

00:12:56.790 --> 00:12:59.990
I’m one of Marshall, Carter, and Dark’s
largest shareholders.

00:12:59.990 --> 00:13:02.899
Amazon is Dr. Wondertainment’s primary global
distributor.

00:13:02.899 --> 00:13:07.220
The Sarkicists, The Fifthists, The Mekhanites,
those pretentious art snobs at Are We Cool

00:13:07.220 --> 00:13:10.040
Yet, they’re all in my deep pockets!”

00:13:10.040 --> 00:13:11.420
Jeff roared.

00:13:11.420 --> 00:13:14.889
He wrapped one of his massive hands around
Dr. Bright’s throat and lifted him clear

00:13:14.889 --> 00:13:16.010
off the ground.

00:13:16.010 --> 00:13:18.040
Jack struggled against his grip.

00:13:18.040 --> 00:13:23.339
“You’ve spent decades worrying about all
the wrong things, Jack,” Jeff said, slowly

00:13:23.339 --> 00:13:25.860
tightening his grip around Dr. Bright’s
throat.

00:13:25.860 --> 00:13:27.339
“The Devourer Of Worlds?

00:13:27.339 --> 00:13:28.339
The Black Moon?

00:13:28.339 --> 00:13:29.339
The Scarlet King?

00:13:29.339 --> 00:13:31.290
My new world won’t have a king.

00:13:31.290 --> 00:13:34.259
It’ll have a CEO.

00:13:34.259 --> 00:13:39.360
And with the power within these walls, I’ll
be the Chairman of the Cosmic Board!

00:13:39.360 --> 00:13:44.879
And it all starts with me killing you and
turning your silly little necklace into a

00:13:44.879 --> 00:13:46.199
paperweight!”

00:13:46.199 --> 00:13:48.800
But Jack had an ace up his sleeve.

00:13:48.800 --> 00:13:52.910
Something he had the good sense to pocket
before facing Bezos on the battlefield.

00:13:52.910 --> 00:13:58.870
He reached into his lab coat and pulled out
SCP-662, The Butler’s Hand Bell.

00:13:58.870 --> 00:14:02.440
One little ring and Mr. Deeds suddenly appeared
right next to them.

00:14:02.440 --> 00:14:07.230
Jack barely managed to wheeze out, “Deeds,
kick Jeff in the groin!”

00:14:07.230 --> 00:14:11.519
“Of course, sir, “ Mr. Deeds said, before
doing exactly that.

00:14:11.519 --> 00:14:15.160
Jeff winced in pain and loosened his grip
on Dr. Bright’s neck.

00:14:15.160 --> 00:14:19.279
The plucky immortal took his chance to wriggle
free from Jeff’s grip and run into the facility,

00:14:19.279 --> 00:14:21.570
yelling back, “Deeds, stall him!”

00:14:21.570 --> 00:14:25.959
But before Deeds could execute this order,
Jeff Bezos fractured the anomalous butler’s

00:14:25.959 --> 00:14:30.250
skull with a single punch, and chased Dr.
Bright into the facility.

00:14:30.250 --> 00:14:32.079
He would have his revenge!

00:14:32.079 --> 00:14:36.620
As Dr. Bright fled, he grabbed his Foundation
walkie-talkie and frantically spoke into it,

00:14:36.620 --> 00:14:37.680
“Clef, I’m in big trouble!

00:14:37.680 --> 00:14:41.410
I think I have a way to stop this, but there’s
just something you need to do for me first...”

00:14:41.410 --> 00:14:43.129
Battles were raging on throughout the site.

00:14:43.129 --> 00:14:47.430
Some Amazon soldiers had unloaded their rifles
into Cain, only to find themselves on the

00:14:47.430 --> 00:14:49.579
floor, dying of massive blood loss.

00:14:49.579 --> 00:14:54.450
Other squadrons of mercenaries were being
tortured by the nightmarish SCP-106 in his

00:14:54.450 --> 00:14:56.050
terrifying pocket dimension.

00:14:56.050 --> 00:14:58.540
He was having a wonderful time.

00:14:58.540 --> 00:15:04.310
SCP-999 was even tickling a gaggle of Amazon’s
hired veteran war criminals into absolute

00:15:04.310 --> 00:15:05.330
submission.

00:15:05.330 --> 00:15:09.709
Much to Jeff’s rage and horror, it looked
like, with the help of the anomalies, the

00:15:09.709 --> 00:15:13.040
Foundation might actually be able to turn
the tide.

00:15:13.040 --> 00:15:14.470
This would not do.

00:15:14.470 --> 00:15:17.420
He’d destroy Bright and take care of the
rest personally.

00:15:17.420 --> 00:15:20.579
“It has to be this way, Jack!”

00:15:20.579 --> 00:15:22.600
Bezos yelled after the fleeing doctor.

00:15:22.600 --> 00:15:26.569
“I’m making the mother of all corporate
omelets here, can’t fret over a few ransacked

00:15:26.569 --> 00:15:28.000
containment sites!”

00:15:28.000 --> 00:15:33.970
Bezos’ self-aggrandizing rants were interrupted
by SCP-682 leaping onto him out of an adjoining

00:15:33.970 --> 00:15:38.440
hallway, giving Dr. Bright even more time
to create distance between them.

00:15:38.440 --> 00:15:44.129
682 fought valiantly and viciously, but Jeff’s
Prometheus Labs nanomachine augmentations

00:15:44.129 --> 00:15:45.850
gave him the edge.

00:15:45.850 --> 00:15:52.120
He was able to get 682 into a headlock, Steve
Irwin style, then punch it in the head until

00:15:52.120 --> 00:15:53.970
it was knocked out.

00:15:53.970 --> 00:15:57.500
Jeff sighed, relieved, and continued the chase
after Jack.

00:15:57.500 --> 00:16:02.110
As Jeff turned a corner to chase Dr. Bright,
he ran right into one of Jack’s traps.

00:16:02.110 --> 00:16:07.010
There was Dr. Bright, standing about fifteen
feet away from him, holding his favorite item

00:16:07.010 --> 00:16:11.329
that he normally wasn’t allowed to use:
The Chainsaw Cannon.

00:16:11.329 --> 00:16:14.600
Jack smirked and said, “Smile, you son of
a—“

00:16:14.600 --> 00:16:15.600
BOOM!

00:16:15.600 --> 00:16:18.269
A chainsaw projectile blasted towards Jeff
at incredible speeds.

00:16:18.269 --> 00:16:22.529
It was through pure luck and superhuman reflexes
that Jeff was able to catch it between his

00:16:22.529 --> 00:16:28.210
palms by the blade and hold it in place, even
as it cut into his nanite-hardened skin.

00:16:28.210 --> 00:16:31.649
With a grunt of rage, he threw the saw to
the ground.

00:16:31.649 --> 00:16:34.829
“Is that all you got, Jack?” he growled.

00:16:34.829 --> 00:16:37.220
“Not quite,” Dr. Bright replied.

00:16:37.220 --> 00:16:40.649
“I’ve got a few friends who owe me some
favors.”

00:16:40.649 --> 00:16:43.120
Suddenly, Bezos heard footsteps behind him.

00:16:43.120 --> 00:16:49.250
He turned to see three figures standing there,
primed and ready for battle: SCP-4494, The

00:16:49.250 --> 00:16:55.209
Specter, SCP-5151 The Black Knight, and SCP-2800,
Cactusman.

00:16:55.209 --> 00:16:58.249
“You fight without honor, Sir Jeffrey!”

00:16:58.249 --> 00:17:00.140
The Black Knight proclaimed as he drew his
longsword.

00:17:00.140 --> 00:17:03.140
“Aye, and I can’t stand bullies!”

00:17:03.140 --> 00:17:05.110
Said Cactusman as his spikes began to grow.

00:17:05.110 --> 00:17:08.289
“Wage theft and tax evasion is a crime,
evildoer!”

00:17:08.289 --> 00:17:09.670
The Specter added.

00:17:09.670 --> 00:17:11.970
“Well, then,” Jeff said.

00:17:11.970 --> 00:17:15.080
“I suppose I’ll just have to kill you
all...”

00:17:15.080 --> 00:17:16.080
The fight began.

00:17:16.080 --> 00:17:20.060
Our group of four heroes held their own impressively,
to begin with.

00:17:20.060 --> 00:17:23.690
They consistently helped each other block
or avoid the deadly strikes that Bezos was

00:17:23.690 --> 00:17:26.100
unleashing and return their own.

00:17:26.100 --> 00:17:28.220
Four anomalies against one.

00:17:28.220 --> 00:17:32.370
The Black Knight even gave Dr. Bright one
of his spare swords to give him a better chance

00:17:32.370 --> 00:17:35.710
of landing a meaningful blow against Bezos.

00:17:35.710 --> 00:17:38.560
But in the end, it was all for nothing.

00:17:38.560 --> 00:17:43.240
Bezos powered up, his nanomachines drawing
energy from the building around him, until

00:17:43.240 --> 00:17:45.070
he was even larger and stronger.

00:17:45.070 --> 00:17:50.540
In his state, he easily beat down his four
attackers, incapacitating them and standing

00:17:50.540 --> 00:17:51.630
over Bright.

00:17:51.630 --> 00:17:55.370
“It’s useless, Jack,” he said with another
evil laugh.

00:17:55.370 --> 00:17:57.120
“You can’t beat me.”

00:17:57.120 --> 00:17:59.390
“I know,” Jack groaned in pain.

00:17:59.390 --> 00:18:02.440
“But I did a pretty good job of stalling
you.”

00:18:02.440 --> 00:18:05.950
At that moment, Clef came running down the
hall, wielding another firearm.

00:18:05.950 --> 00:18:08.310
But it wasn’t a shotgun this time.

00:18:08.310 --> 00:18:13.860
In fact, it didn’t even look like a real
gun, it looked like a spray-painted Nerf gun.

00:18:13.860 --> 00:18:15.910
That got another laugh out of Jeff.

00:18:15.910 --> 00:18:17.660
What an utterly feeble attempt.

00:18:17.660 --> 00:18:22.170
That’s when Dr. Clef leveled the nerf gun
and fired one of its darts at Jeff’s chest,

00:18:22.170 --> 00:18:24.850
where it seemed to bounce off uselessly.

00:18:24.850 --> 00:18:25.850
“Really?”

00:18:25.850 --> 00:18:26.910
He asked, incredulous.

00:18:26.910 --> 00:18:27.950
“Come on.

00:18:27.950 --> 00:18:29.000
This is just getting—“

00:18:29.000 --> 00:18:32.400
His words were cut off by an uppercut from
Dr. Bright.

00:18:32.400 --> 00:18:34.780
Inexplicably, he actually felt that one.

00:18:34.780 --> 00:18:37.990
Jeff staggered back, rubbing his jaw as Bright
rose to his feet.

00:18:37.990 --> 00:18:40.120
“How the hell did you hurt me?”

00:18:40.120 --> 00:18:41.850
Jeff muttered, genuinely shocked.

00:18:41.850 --> 00:18:42.930
Dr. Bright smirked.

00:18:42.930 --> 00:18:45.260
“That was the Nerfing Gun, chrome dome.

00:18:45.260 --> 00:18:47.940
We just made your precious nanomachines useless.”

00:18:47.940 --> 00:18:52.050
With another incredibly well-earned punch
in the face from Dr. Bright, Jeff was down

00:18:52.050 --> 00:18:54.300
on the ground with a bleeding nose.

00:18:54.300 --> 00:18:57.790
Elsewhere in the facility, the researchers,
guards, and anomalies working together had

00:18:57.790 --> 00:18:59.950
defeated the dark forces of Amazon.

00:18:59.950 --> 00:19:05.400
Outside, Hammer Down - The largest and most
militarily powerful Mobile Task Force - had

00:19:05.400 --> 00:19:09.260
arrived and wiped out what remained of Jeff’s
invasion force outside.

00:19:09.260 --> 00:19:12.980
It wasn’t easy, but the SCP Foundation had
won.

00:19:12.980 --> 00:19:17.940
As Jeff lay on the ground, holding his broken
nose, Dr. Bright held him at sword point.

00:19:17.940 --> 00:19:20.170
“Wait, Wait!” Jeff said.

00:19:20.170 --> 00:19:22.080
“Let’s not let hard feelings linger.

00:19:22.080 --> 00:19:23.080
We’re both adults, right?

00:19:23.080 --> 00:19:24.080
And I’m a businessman.

00:19:24.080 --> 00:19:25.080
I make deals.

00:19:25.080 --> 00:19:26.080
Compromises.

00:19:26.080 --> 00:19:27.880
I can give you anything from the Amazon stock,
free of charge!

00:19:27.880 --> 00:19:30.750
As long as we agree that I can go and we forget
all this!”

00:19:30.750 --> 00:19:32.950
Dr. Bright smiled and thought it over.

00:19:32.950 --> 00:19:34.620
“Well...” he said.

00:19:34.620 --> 00:19:37.790
“There are a few things I think I’d like
for myself.

00:19:37.790 --> 00:19:41.390
And there are still plenty more anomalies
that need enriching...”

00:19:41.390 --> 00:19:42.730
Victory secured.

00:19:42.730 --> 00:19:46.690
Want another video abo but the deranged things
Dr. Bright bought for even more anomalies

00:19:46.690 --> 00:19:48.230
and Foundation staff?

00:19:48.230 --> 00:19:52.520
Let us know down in the comments, and we’ll
continue the strangest story that the SCP

00:19:52.520 --> 00:19:55.800
Foundation’s most eccentric researcher ever
told...

00:19:55.800 --> 00:20:00.580
Now go check out “SCP Edition - Weird Things
On Amazon - Dr. Bright’s Great Idea!”

00:20:00.580 --> 00:20:06.040
and “SCP-001 When Day Breaks Dr. Bright”
for more of the mad doctor’s most peculiar

00:20:06.040 --> 00:20:06.340
adventures!

